config SERVICE_AUDIO_COMPANION
    bool "Audio companion background streaming"
    depends on MIC && SERVICE_VOICE
    select AUDIO_COMPANION_SERVICE_ENABLED if BT_FW_NIMBLE
    select MBEDTLS
    select MIC_SF32LB_CAPTURE_DEEP_WFI if MIC_SF32LB
    help
      Background microphone streaming to an authorized third-party audio
      companion app over a dedicated watch-hosted GATT service. The
      transport requires a NimBLE Bluetooth backend; on other backends the
      service compiles but stays inert.

      MBEDTLS is selected for the receiver registry's SHA-256 (see
      pebble_mbedtls_config.h, which enables the primitive only when this
      symbol is set). NimBLE selects it too; the select makes the
      dependency hold on the other backends as well.

      MIC_SF32LB_CAPTURE_DEEP_WFI is selected because a background
      recorder keeps the microphone open for hours at a time: without it
      the core cannot sleep deeper than plain WFI at full clock for the
      whole of that, which is the single largest power cost of the feature.

if SERVICE_AUDIO_COMPANION

module = SERVICE_AUDIO_COMPANION
module-str = Audio companion
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

config AUDIO_COMPANION_SPOOL_MIN_BYTES
    int "Audio companion spool floor (bytes)"
    default 8192
    help
      The spool may always grow to at least this many bytes of encoded
      audio, regardless of heap pressure.

config AUDIO_COMPANION_SPOOL_MAX_BYTES
    int "Audio companion spool ceiling (bytes)"
    default 131072
    help
      Hard upper bound on opportunistic spool memory. The spool may grow toward
      this ceiling only while the kernel heap reserve below is still available;
      on tighter devices the effective capacity is lower.

config AUDIO_COMPANION_SPOOL_HEAP_RESERVE_BYTES
    int "Kernel heap headroom the spool must always leave free"
    default 32768
    help
      The spool only grows while at least this much kernel heap stays free after
      another chunk-sized allocation, and sheds optional chunks when free heap
      drops below it.

config AUDIO_COMPANION_LOW_BATTERY_PERCENT
    int "Pause streaming below this battery percent"
    default 20

endif # SERVICE_AUDIO_COMPANION
